-- title:
--   The FLT adelic genus equals the Riemann–Roch genus of a function field
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field and let $K/k$ be an algebraic function field in one variable, presented through a separating variable: $K$ is a finite separable extension of the rational function field $k(X)$, the structure maps $k\to k[X]\to k(X)\to K$ being compatible. Assume that $k$ is the full constant field of $K$: every element of $K$ that is algebraic over $k$ already lies in $k$. Assume moreover that $k$ is a perfect field.
--
--   The genus $g(K)$ of the Riemann–Roch library is the largest value of $\deg D+1-\ell(D)$ over all divisors $D$ of $K/k$, where places are valuation rings $k\subseteq\mathcal O_P\subsetneq K$ with infinite cyclic value group, $\deg P=[\mathcal O_P/\mathfrak m_P:k]$, and $\ell(D)=\dim_k\{f\in K: f=0\ \text{or}\ v_P(f)\ge -D(P)\ \forall P\}$. The FLT genus is defined adelically: let $\mathbb A$ be the ring of répartitions of $K/k$ in the FLT sense, the $K$-subalgebra of $\prod_v K$ (product over the FLT places $v$) generated by the families $(\alpha_v)$ with $\alpha_v\in\mathcal O_v$ for all but finitely many $v$; let $\mathbb A(0)=\{\alpha\in\mathbb A:\ \alpha_v\in\mathcal O_v\ \text{for all } v\}$, and embed $K$ diagonally. The FLT genus is
--   $$g^{\mathrm{FLT}}(K)=\dim_k\ \mathbb A\big/\big(\mathbb A(0)+K\big).$$ Here the FLT places $v$ are the valuation rings $k\subseteq\mathcal O_v\subsetneq K$ that are discrete valuation rings (these are exactly the valuation rings of the places above). Then
--   $$g^{\mathrm{FLT}}(K)=g(K).$$
--
--   This identifies the genus used by the FLT algebraic-curve API (for instance in the existence of the $L$-polynomial and in the Riemann hypothesis for curves over finite fields) with the genus computed by the Riemann–Roch library.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The tower $k\to k[X]\to k(X)\to K$ is given by the instances `Algebra k[X] K`, `Algebra k⟮X⟯ K`, `Algebra k K`, `IsScalarTower k k[X] K` and `IsScalarTower k[X] k⟮X⟯ K`, together with `FunctionField k K` ($K$ is finite-dimensional over $k(X)$) and `Algebra.IsSeparable k⟮X⟯ K`. The full constant field hypothesis is `FunctionField.IsFullConstantField k K`, and `[PerfectField k]` is an explicit hypothesis of the theorem (a standing assumption of the FLT genus API). The FLT genus is `AlgebraicCurve.genusFF k K = Module.finrank k (H1 0)`, with `H1 0` the quotient of `repartitions k K` by `repartitionsOf 0 ⊔ principalRepartitions k K`; the library genus `FunctionField.genus k K` is the natural-number truncation of the supremum of the defects.
-- source:
--   Comparison of two definitions of the genus: H. Stichtenoth, *Algebraic Function Fields and Codes*, 2nd ed., GTM 254, Springer 2009, Definition 1.4.15 (genus as maximal defect) and Section 1.5, Corollary 1.5.5 ($g=\dim_K \mathcal A_F/(\mathcal A_F(0)+F)$). Lean: bridge written for this port, file `Bridge/RiemannRochFLT.lean`

